# ChapterFlow — local development env template.
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in. Never commit secret values.
# Full env-var matrix + resolution order: docs/ENVIRONMENT.md
#
# Zero-AWS dev needs NO env file at all: `npm run dev` bakes in
# DEV_AUTH_BYPASS=1 and all localhost URLs. This template is only for hitting
# REAL data (the dev catalog/library in AWS) from a local server.

# --- AWS credentials (resolved via the default SDK credential chain) --------
# Alternative: skip these and use a ~/.aws profile (e.g. AWS_PROFILE=chapterflow).
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Only needed for temporary/SSO (STS) credentials:
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# Code defaults to us-east-1; set only if your resources live elsewhere:
# AWS_REGION=

# --- Data plane: EITHER the SSM prefix OR the four explicit names -----------
# Option A (recommended): one prefix; the server resolves names from SSM.
SSM_PARAMETER_PREFIX=/chapterflow/dev
# Option B: explicit resource names (leave Option A unset if using these).
# BOOK_TABLE_NAME=
# BOOK_ANALYTICS_TABLE_NAME=
# BOOK_CONTENT_BUCKET=
# BOOK_INGEST_BUCKET=

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Local admin gate for the in-app admin panels:
# ADMIN_EMAILS=
# ADMIN_SUBS=
# Only to exercise the AI features locally (Ask the Book, reflection feedback,
# scenario validation) — they degrade gracefully without it:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
